197	## 2. Library Decisions + Reasoning
198	
199	### 2a. Signature Pad — `react-signature-canvas@1.0.6`
200	
201	| Candidate | Touch | SVG export | PNG export | Pressure | Bundle | Verdict |
202	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
203	| `react-signature-canvas` | Yes | Via path | `toDataURL('image/png')` | No (not needed) | ~14 KB | **PICK** |
204	| `signature_pad` (vanilla) | Yes | Via path | Yes | Yes | ~9 KB | Runner-up (no React wrapper) |
205	| `react-sketchy` | Yes | No | Yes | No | ~22 KB | Overkill |
206	| `perfect-freehand` + canvas | Yes | Manual | Manual | Yes | ~6 KB | Too manual |
207	
208	**Why `react-signature-canvas`:** Direct React ref API (`sigPad.getTrimmedCanvas()`, `sigPad.toDataURL()`), production-tested, handles mouse/touch/stylus uniformly, easy to disable/clear/check-empty. SVG export: iterate `_data` property to generate an SVG path string from the stored points array.
209	
210	**Minimum valid signature:** Check `sigPad.isEmpty()` AND count total points across all strokes `>= 20`. A single dot fails both checks.
211	
212	**Install:**
213	```bash
214	pnpm add react-signature-canvas
215	pnpm add -D @types/react-signature-canvas
216	```
217	
218	### 2b. Drag-Reorder — `@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`
219	
220	Already the InkOS standard. Use `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy` and `DragOverlay` for the ghost preview. No new install needed if Sprint 3/4 installed them. Verify:
221	```bash
222	pnpm list @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable
223	```
224	If missing: `pnpm add @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable @dnd-kit/utilities`
225	
226	### 2c. Markdown Renderer — `react-markdown` + `rehype-sanitize`
227	
228	```bash
229	pnpm add react-markdown rehype-sanitize
230	```
231	Used only in section body rendering (template preview + public signing page). Never in the edit form (that's a plain `<Textarea>`). Allowed elements: `p strong em ul ol li a br`. Strip everything else via `rehype-sanitize` with a custom schema.
232	
233	### 2d. PDF Generation — `@react-pdf/renderer` in BullMQ worker
234	
235	```bash
236	# In workers/ package.json only — never in the Next.js app
237	pnpm add @react-pdf/renderer
238	```
239	
240	PDF is generated server-side (worker) after submission. Design: A4 portrait, studio logo top-right, template title as heading, sections rendered in order, signature image embedded as PNG, audit metadata at bottom, watermark "SIGNED COPY — [studio name]" at 5% opacity diagonal. Stored to Supabase Storage `consent-pdfs/[studio_id]/[submission_id].pdf`. Signed URL generated on each download request (1-hour TTL).
241	
242	**Do NOT use jsPDF or html2canvas.** `@react-pdf/renderer` gives deterministic layout and is worker-safe (no DOM dependency).
